WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.280
 People always ask us
what advertising is.

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:03.570
It's a business of rejection.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.650
You have to expect it.

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.330
 Every damn day.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:07.250
 Every day.

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:10.680
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:16.800
 I think advertising
is like vandalism.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.877
It's loud, in your face, and
it's still there the next day.

00:00:20.877 --> 00:00:22.460
 If someone says,
this is going to be

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.260
really funny, don't do that.

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:25.880
Don't tell people how to feel.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:26.400
Let them--

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:26.900
 Yeah.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:29.420
 --feel through what you have.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:32.720
Brands are allowed to
have a social conscience.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.668
With Doritos, we did rainbow
chips for a gay pride parade.

00:00:37.668 --> 00:00:39.710
And I think that's what's
changed in advertising.

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:43.100
You're allowed to bring
the social commentary

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.580
into the brand.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.170
That's a big deal.

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:48.770
And we're going to talk
about a 30-second film.

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:49.719
 Bud

00:00:49.719 --> 00:00:50.219
 Weise

00:00:50.219 --> 00:00:51.185
 [SCREAMS]

00:00:51.185 --> 00:00:52.151
 [SCREAMS]

00:00:52.151 --> 00:00:53.117
[WHOOSH]

00:00:53.117 --> 00:00:55.040
[PHONE RINGS]

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:55.540
 Hello?

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:56.457
MAN (ON PHONE): Hello.

00:00:56.457 --> 00:00:57.793
For $10,000, who--

00:00:57.793 --> 00:00:59.303
 Aaron Burr.

00:00:59.303 --> 00:01:01.970
Any commercial
starts with finding the truth--

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:02.780
 Aaron Burr.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.370
 --within the problem.

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:07.610
 We weren't motivated to
drink more milk by knowing

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:08.720
that it was good for us.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:09.740
Your mom told you that.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:11.195
 Milk!

00:01:11.195 --> 00:01:13.310
MAN (ON PHONE): I'm afraid
your time is almost up.

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:15.680
 That was the whole
campaign, was making people

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:17.300
afraid to run out of milk.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.340
 Aaron Burr.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:20.563
ANNOUNCER: Got milk?

00:01:20.563 --> 00:01:21.980
JEFF GOODBY: A lot
of people think

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:24.110
that advertising is telling
somebody something that

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:26.400
isn't true, but getting
them to believe it.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.910
That's not what we do.

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:30.500
RICH SILVERSTEIN: We understand
it's art serving capitalism.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:34.430
But we want to be artists
in a business world.

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:36.140
Advertising is so fluid.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:38.210
There is no
consistency that, this

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:39.890
is what you should be doing.

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:42.230
The key is to be fearless.

00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:44.090
You're not going to
be right all the time.

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:46.382
Just put your heart into
something you feel good about.

00:01:46.382 --> 00:01:48.173
JEFF GOODBY: You have
to have a little fire

00:01:48.173 --> 00:01:51.560
burning inside yourself, and you
have to be open to the world.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:52.790
 Come and challenge us.

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:54.010
We want it.

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:55.205
 Bring it.

00:01:55.205 --> 00:01:55.890
Hi, I'm Goodby.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:57.150
 And I'm Silverstein.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.880
 And this is our MasterClass.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.230
[MUSIC PLAYING]

